# Coach speech (Turkish): the rules lesson (level 0, src/coach/lesson.cpp).
# Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/lesson.lang.
#
# Placeholders: {your} / {my} = a piece of the player / of the coach ("kalen", "atım"), with the forms
# of common.lang ({my:acc} atımı, {my:dat} atıma, {my:gen} atımın, {your:ins} kalenle ...);
# {sq}, {sq2}, {to}, {esc} = squares, never followed by a suffix: the case goes on the noun "kare"
# ("{sq} karesine", "{sq} karesindeki"); {move} = a move. {@}, {@2}, {@3} are invisible marks: the
# coach points at something while saying the word right after the mark. A ".spoken" key is what the
# voice says instead (here: Latin letters said with their Turkish letter names, "he", "le").
# Files = dikey, ranks = yatay, back rank = son yatay (glossary). Squares are "attacked" in the
# sense of "tehdit etmek" ("{my} o kareyi tehdit ediyor").

# ---- Chapter titles (said inside "Şimdi {chapter} ile devam edelim.") ---------------------------------
# Nominative, lower case (see event.lesson.* in events.lang).
